{"_id":"6a2ff59d2204ffbc59e5a639","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"10c4tiBOR68J3qa55LcJS","description":"# APIs with requests\n\nThe `requests` library is the standard Python tool for making HTTP requests. It is used to call REST APIs that return JSON or XML data. A typical workflow involves calling `requests.get(url, params=params)`, checking the response status, and parsing the JSON body with `.json()` before loading it into a DataFrame.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Python Requests Module","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/python/module_requests.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebc9"},{"type":"article","title":"Python's Requests Library (Guide)","url":"https://realpython.com/python-requests/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebca"},{"type":"video","title":"Master Python Requests In 15 Minutes. Call Any API","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xnbef8F_Yfc","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebcb"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:52:45.738Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/10c4tiBOR68J3qa55LcJS.md"}